as risk factors for ischemic heart disease. Results from the Qu&#x000e9;bec Cardiovascular Study</article-title><source>Atherosclerosis</source><year>1996</year><volume>119</volume><fpage>235</fpage><lpage>45</lpage><pub-id pub-id-type="pmid">8808500</pub-id></citation></ref><ref id="b25"><citation citation-type="journal"><person-group person-group-type="author"><name><surname>Lamarche</surname><given-names>B</given-names></name><name><surname>Rashid</surname><given-names>S</given-names></name><name><surname>Lewis</surname><given-names>GF</given-names></name></person-group><article-title>HDL metabolism in hypertriglyceridemic states: an overview</article-title><source>Clin Chim Acta</source><year>1999</year><volume>286</volume><fpage>145</fpage><lpage>61</lpage><pub-id pub-id-type="pmid">10511289</pub-id></citation></ref><ref id="b26"><citation citation-type="journal"><person-group person-group-type="author"><name><surname>Le</surname><given-names>NA</given-names></name><name><surname>Ginsberg</surname><given-names>HN</given-names></name></person-group><article-title>Heterogeneity of apolipoprotein A-I turnover in subjects with reduced concentrations of plasma high density lipoprotein cholesterol</article-title><source>Metabolism</source><year>1988</year><volume>37</volume><fpage>614</fpage><lpage>17</lpage><pub-id pub-id-type="pmid">3133537</pub-id></citation></ref><ref id="b27"><citation citation-type="journal"><person-group person-group-type="author"><name><surname>Maron</surname><given-names>DJ</given-names></name></person-group><article-title>The epidemiology of low levels of high-density lipoprotein cholesterol in patients with and without coronary artery disease</article-title><source>Am J Cardiol</source><year>2000</year><volume>86</volume><fpage>11L</fpage><lpage>14L</lpage></citation></ref><ref id="b28"><citation citation-type="journal"><person-group person-group-type="author"><name><surname>Mercuro</surname><given-names>G</given-names></name><name><surnam